    "body": "## Summary\n- block `SUSPENDED` transitions through the generic admin user-status endpoint\n- require account suspensions to use the reviewed-report enforcement workflow with its lifecycle safeguards and immutable audit\n- keep generic status changes as a narrow recovery path for reactivating an already suspended non-admin account\n- remove the direct \"Zawieś\" control from the admin users list and point active-user sanctions to the moderation queue\n- add regression tests for suspension rejection, valid reactivation and active-account no-op rejection\n- document the enforcement boundary\n\n## Why\nThe existing `/admin/users/{id}/status` endpoint could suspend a user directly, bypassing the newly added reviewed-report requirement, protected active-job checks, open-listing cleanup and enforcement audit. This PR closes that alternate path.\n\n## Validation\nRun Maven verify, frontend lint/build and the existing container/runtime gates. Do not merge unless required checks are green.",
