            "patch_url": "https://github.com/jedreekPrograms/dofast/pull/59.patch",
            "merged_at": "2026-08-27T15:05:16Z"
          },
          "body": "## Summary\n- add Flyway V28 for immutable admin account reactivation audits\n- persist the target user, acting administrator, previous/new status and timestamp whenever a suspended account is reactivated\n- keep suspension itself restricted to the reviewed-report enforcement workflow\n- extend AdminUserService regression tests to require an audit row for successful recovery and no audit for rejected status changes\n\n## Safety\nThis change does not create a new suspension path and does not touch escrow, job lifecycle or location data. It closes the remaining audit gap in the narrow generic admin recovery path introduced by #58.\n\n## Validation\nRun Maven verify, frontend lint/build and existing runtime/smoke gates. Do not merge unless required checks are green.",
          "reactions": {
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jedreekPrograms/dofast/issues/59/reactions",
